# reac-pw-phc2sys@<nic>.service: keep <nic>'s PTP hardware clock on CLOCK_TAI, so the NIC
# can launch REAC frames at their SCM_TXTIME (reac-pw's hardware launch, reac-pw#98).
#
#   systemctl enable --now reac-pw-phc2sys@reac0.service
#
# WHY. Under the hardware launch (mqprio + etf offload, on an i210/i225/i226) the NIC holds
# each frame until its OWN clock reaches the frame's launch time, which reac-pw writes in
# CLOCK_TAI. A PHC nobody aligns runs free from whatever it read at boot, and the NIC then
# holds frames for the wrong instant: the queue fills and sendmsg fails, thousands a second
# (an i226 bench 2026-11-15, one port: tx_errors 4000/s and every TX stamp unpaired). reac-pw reads
# the PHC against CLOCK_TAI before it installs the hardware form and takes the software
# form, saying so, when they are more than 1 ms apart, so this unit is what makes the
# hardware form possible; it is never what makes audio possible.
#
# ONE OWNER OF THE PHC. Where ptp4l runs on this NIC (AES67), ptp4l owns the PHC and its
# own phc2sys aligns the SYSTEM clock to it; this unit must not also steer the PHC, so it
# refuses to start there. Elsewhere this unit owns it: the source is the system clock
# (chrony), the sink is the PHC.
#
# -O 37: the PHC carries TAI, the system clock UTC; 37 s is the TAI-UTC offset in force
#   since 2017 (the kernel's own adjtimex offset on a chrony-disciplined host reads the
#   same). If it is ever wrong reac-pw reads the PHC a second or more off TAI and refuses
#   the hardware form, by name.
# -S 0.00002: STEP the PHC when it is more than 20 us off. igc RESETS the adapter whenever
#   the launch queue's qdisc changes, and the reset can move the PHC; without a step
#   threshold phc2sys only steps at start and would slew for minutes.
# Restart=always: the same reset makes PTP_SYS_OFFSET_PRECISE time out, and phc2sys EXITS
#   on that (an i226 bench 2026-11-15, both ports, at the first install). Restarted, it re-steps.
[Unit]
Description=Align %I's PTP hardware clock to CLOCK_TAI (reac-pw hardware launch)
Documentation=man:phc2sys(8) https://github.com/FreeREAC/reac-pw
After=chronyd.service time-sync.target sys-subsystem-net-devices-%i.device
BindsTo=sys-subsystem-net-devices-%i.device
Conflicts=ptp4l@%i.service

[Service]
Type=simple
# Refuse where ptp4l already runs on this NIC: two writers on one PHC fight.
ExecCondition=/bin/sh -c '! pgrep -f "ptp4l .*-i %I( |$)" >/dev/null'
ExecStart=/usr/sbin/phc2sys -s CLOCK_REALTIME -c %I -O 37 -R 8 -S 0.00002 -m -q
Restart=always
RestartSec=1

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
